#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:5
#: f2054259b7aa4ac8acd37b9df99cf08c
msgid "Elevon Planes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:10
#: 838a12d7b3754256bfeb82c515f5e821
msgid "Elevon planes (also known as delta-wings) are popular for their simplicity and robustness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:13
#: db3f755828b94ab08326f2c5946492d9
msgid "A typical elevon plane will have 2 servo outputs and one throttle output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:17
#: 06d4aa16eb4c46af8dc7c07ff62e7980
msgid "Setting Up Your Plane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:19
#: 04f24f60814a4efd83b705325fd8a0e2
msgid "The recommended setup for APM:Plane with elevon planes is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:30
#: 0d4cfa8ed8fb4eb199a83ff3444a239f
msgid "You should remove the propeller from your aircraft before starting your setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:34
#: 75eacacdb3bb42898999785604c5fe54
msgid "RC Input Setup & Reversal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:36
#: e1e1840137e34445a0ad1edfa7b9793b
msgid "Set up your :ref:`RC inputs <rc-throw-trim>` through the calibration process, and verify them for reversal. Reversals are critical to the process. Commanding pitch up and roll right must result in higher PWM values for RCn_in channels. If the value does not respond correctly reverse the channel before continuing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:42
#: 3a0d243b90c840c7a77425eef3f06a2a
msgid "You can connect your 3 servo cables to any output of your autopilot, although using the defaults listed above is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:46
#: f0486c7c7e5a4c0ebc8204e8e4e3f1fb
msgid "Servo Setup & Reversal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:48
#: 54a79d61956b49099d8890a8ce9f84cb
msgid "The next step is to get the servo reversals right. You should connect the battery (with propeller removed) and turn on your RC transmitter. Now switch to FBWA mode and press the safety switch (if fitted) to enable servo outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:53
#: 74fe21fc27f64d3098ffbf5c76aa6ea5
msgid "At this point both the autopilot and RC transmitter should have control of the elevons. You now should adjust the reversal and function of the two servos so that you get correct movement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:57
#: a107c3762eb8422d8376ce46b985eece
msgid "Correct FBWA (automatic stabilization)movement for an elevon plane WITHOUT PROVIDING RC INPUT is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:70
#: b0249d72bfbe4005948421a272025edc
msgid "If your movements are incorrect then you need to adjust which servo output is left/right and the reversals of each elevon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:73
#: a23493a10e0f456b9fdc608a2e6f31f7
msgid "The parameters you should adjust are :ref:`SERVO1_REVERSED<SERVO1_REVERSED>`, :ref:`SERVO2_REVERSED<SERVO2_REVERSED>`, :ref:`SERVO1_FUNCTION<SERVO1_FUNCTION>` and :ref:`SERVO2_FUNCTION<SERVO2_FUNCTION>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:76
#: 652e48768d48487782075cb939b89ff9
msgid "If your left elevon on servo 1 is moving the wrong way for both pitch and roll corrections, set :ref:`SERVO1_REVERSED<SERVO1_REVERSED>` to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:79
#: b961baec72e9427d9d605649058b5dcc
msgid "If your left elevon on servo 1 responds correctly to pitch, but incorrectly to roll, change the :ref:`SERVO1_FUNCTION<SERVO1_FUNCTION>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:82
#: 3d7e90e3104e4e499bbbc571ed877913
msgid "Repeat the servo reversal or function change for the right elevon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:84
#: b69d8aa7ff6a48e59040a6d9887ac0df
msgid "In rare instances, both servo 1 and 2 will individually respond correctly with the same FUNCTION. This is OK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:87
#: c723f17f347f475eb354d8f1056cbba8
msgid "while rolling the aircraft the autopilot will automatically try to put in some up pitch, as it knows that upward pitch is needed in turns. So you will probably see an asymmetry in elevon movement. The elevon that is going down will not go down very far, or (depending on your settings) may not go down at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:95
#: 5c38f83a3a4e49288bebc89daea7f96a
msgid "Verify RC Inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:97
#: e3f59284440c49dd91025dca03b8fbe9
msgid "Now that the elevons are configured correctly, verify your RC inputs. In FBWA with the airplane level, command pitch-up from your transmitter and confirm that the elevons both rise. Command a roll to the right from your transmitter and confirm that the right elevon rises and the left elevon lowers. If this is incorrect, read the :ref:`RC inputs <rc-throw-trim>` page to fix your rc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:104
#: 81f376b394d1474a8b774e20c100bc95
msgid "Switch the plane to MANUAL mode and confirm the same behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:107
#: 0642324cfbbf41039f687a1075b3bc6d
msgid "Servo Trim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:109
#: 537d8ff321f84e01b5fd74839470c266
msgid "Now stay in MANUAL mode in order to adjust the servo trim values. The servo trim is in the SERVOn_TRIM parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:112
#: a031484e6fb7481c8fefc7b7f3730421
msgid "You should adjust the trim values so that the servo is centered when your transmitter sticks are centered. If you find you need to adjust the trim value by more than 50 PWM from the default of 1500 then it is recommended that you instead adjust the trim mechanically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:118
#: a19785ef1a214776b8c5d8d829960261
msgid "Servo Throw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:120
#: 5f2b6bf6d32243ad88d410ba4be83a7a
msgid "Finally you should adjust your servo throw. The throw is the range of movement for each of your servos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:123
#: 23d0770c0d3b4ed1b607a3716c9301fc
msgid "Check any instructions that came with your plane for suggested throw values. These are often specified in millimeters or inches of movement of the edge of the control surface. If your aircraft doesn't come with any suggested throw values then choose a throw that doesn't cause your servos to \"bind\" (which is indicated by a high pitched sound when your servos move too far)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:130
#: 4e99cdb9c84149f6957fdfb594e2fefb
msgid "To adjust the throw, change the SERVOn_MIN and SERVOn_MAX values. The defaults are 1100 to 1900. On many aircraft you will want more throw than that, and can change to a throw of 1000 to 2000."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:135
#: 803035e2e21e4461ad62015ab890c13f
msgid "Mixing Gain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:137
#: 4c3057be59eb4e46ad80aceaab8b4c06
msgid "The :ref:`MIXING_GAIN<MIXING_GAIN>` parameter is critical for elevon aircraft. It is the gain used in mixing between roll and pitch input and your elevon movement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:141
#: 7414e75c39c04da8926d0a9b0421c7f7
msgid "For example, if your :ref:`MIXING_GAIN<MIXING_GAIN>` is 0.5, then the following outputs are used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:144
#: ee7a14bf57ce409f92196964868caeac
msgid "LEFT ELEVON = (roll+pitch)*0.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:145
#: efac6fb56192492bb0512d0bd286c917
msgid "RIGHT ELEVON = (roll-pitch)*0.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:147
#: c518622cbb83452fb5fc5a197b83468a
msgid "So, simultaneous full roll and  full pitch input will result in maximum travel of the elevons if mixing gain is 0.5. But if just full roll or pitch is input, maximum elevon deflection would be only 50%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:149
#: a90dedb3dc8b42e5b27f3f7f379d1ed1
msgid "If more deflection is desired when using only one control input, the mixing gain can be increased. However, with gains above 0.5, surface deflection will be saturated at some point when both inputs are simultaneously applied. For example, if you use a gain of 1.0, and apply full roll, you will obtain the maximum elevon deflection possible to produce roll. But then adding in pitch while holding full roll input, will reduce the effective roll deflection because one elevon deflection is already saturated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:152
#: 79091d5ff5b644e3af8ae5fd32c8db6c
msgid "Mixing Offset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:154
#: 61eb6b076ad5421095aa83afe5b5a15f
msgid "The :ref:`MIXING_OFFSET<MIXING_OFFSET>` parameter allows increasing the sensitivity of either roll or pitch inputs by effectively multiplying the stick input. A value between -1000 and +1000 can be used, with 0 having no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:156
#: 76d5f2ab98f4463a82a972b072c1a63e
msgid "If a negative value is used, the pitch input is multiplied, while the roll input is unaffected. If  positive, only roll is affected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:158
#: 299667ea0f944d128001091cba367eff
msgid "The amount the stick input value is multiplied is given by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:160
#: 5a0f316c2d1a40f79aa8faa404b6d65e
msgid "Multiplier in % = 100 + | :ref:`MIXING_OFFSET<MIXING_OFFSET>` |"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-elevon-plane.rst:162
#: 993295243db744059953f5da10a32d5e
msgid "So, if :ref:`MIXING_OFFSET<MIXING_OFFSET>` = 100 then roll inputs will be multiplied by 2...so when the aileron stick is deflected halfway, full throw will be effectively input.CAUTION: Roll stick inputs above half will have no further effect."
msgstr ""

